        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಸಸ್ಯ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಸ್ಯ — sasya — \"vegetation; a plant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಈ ಬೆಟ್ಟದಲ್ಲಿ ಅಪರೂಪದ ಸಸ್ಯಗಳು ಬೆಳೆಯುತ್ತವೆ. ī beṭṭadalli aparūpada sasyagaḷu beḷeyuttave. Rare plants grow on this hill."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ಸಸ್ಯಗಳು, sasyagaḷu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A word of science and botany; ಗಿಡ is the everyday plant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಸ್ಯ (sasya) is borrowed from Sanskrit sasya, \"grain, fruit, crops\" (CDIAL 13295); Kannada uses it for plants in general."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
